%% Agent run request lifecycle
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant C as Client
  participant G as Agent Gateway
  participant O as Orchestrator (Temporal)
  participant D as Memory / RAG (pgvector)
  participant S as SGLang Router → Engine
  participant T as MCP Tools (sandbox)

  C->>G: POST /v1/agents/{agent}/runs (SSE stream)
  G->>O: authenticate · quota check · start durable run
  O->>D: load session + hybrid retrieval + tool schemas
  D-->>O: context pack (docs · episodic memory · policies)

  loop until final answer or budget exhausted
    O->>S: chat/completions with tools[] + JSON-schema grammar, streaming
    S-->>O: tokens + tool_call (guaranteed-valid structured output)
    O->>T: invoke tool via MCP (sandboxed pod if untrusted)
    T-->>O: observation / tool result
    O->>D: persist step · update memory (async via JetStream)
    Note over O: guardrail checks on every LLM input/output + one OTel span per step
  end

  O->>G: final answer stream + citations + usage report
  G->>C: SSE tokens → final message · audit log · cost metering
